  {"id": "F2", "category": "definition-mismatch", "severity": "low", "decl": "WordHyperbolic", "line": 24, "paper_ref": "Theorem 1.1", "explanation": "Thinness is required only at vertices of the Cayley graph, using graph distance and geodesic walks. Points interior to edges are ignored, which is standard up to a shift δ ↦ δ+1. Faithfulness also relies on `SimpleGraph.mulCayley` having the usual Cayley-graph adjacency (left or right multiplication by elements of S, symmetrized).", "polarity": "unclear", "probe_idea": "Check the definition of SimpleGraph.mulCayley: prove `(SimpleGraph.mulCayley S).Adj a b ↔ a ≠ b ∧ ∃ s ∈ S, a * s = b ∨ b * s = a` (or the left-multiplication analogue)."}
 ],
